```
LOGIC API PROTOTYPE — README

Modular JavaScript functions usable as:

  • Client-side Service Worker APIs
  • Network-visible fetch endpoints
  • Bun CLI scripts
  • Cloudflare Workers (per function or unified router)

Ref: chat.openai.com/c/6854ee46-4a54-800c-bf40-357cdbb17d19

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TEST LOCALLY

-- 1. HTML + Service Worker (with visible /api/*.js calls) --

  python3 -m http.server
  open http://localhost:8000

  -> click "Run" to test
  -> inspect DevTools > Network tab for /api/add.js, etc.


-- 2. CLI (Bun) --

  bun run api/add.js --a=1 --b=2
  bun run api/calculateArea.js --width=4 --height=3 --margin=1


-- 3. Cloudflare Worker (Per Function) --

  wrangler dev api/add.js
  curl "http://127.0.0.1:8787/?a=1&b=2"

  # change wrangler.toml 'main' as needed


-- 4. Cloudflare Worker (All APIs via api/index.js router) --

  wrangler dev api/index.js
  curl "http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/multiply.js?x=3&y=4"
  curl "http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/calculateArea.js?width=3&height=3&margin=1"

  # wrangler.toml:
  #   main = "api/index.js"


-- 5. Remote Usage (Other Origin / DevTools Console) --

  fetch("https://yourhost.com/api/add.js?a=5&b=10").then(r => r.json())


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

USAGE NOTES

- Logic modules are in /api/*.js and export named functions
- /lib/ contains shared CLI + Worker helpers
- Supports: fetch(), Bun, and Cloudflare natively
- Static imports in Service Worker = spec-compliant + visible

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
```
